  "body": [
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_1",
        "label": "YGas 1"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "svadharmajñānavairāgyasādhyabhaktyekagocaraḥ |",
          "segment_number": 1,
          "translated_text": "<s>Nārāyaṇa</s>, the supreme <s>Brahman</s>, who is the sole object of <s>bhakti</s> (devotion) attainable through one's own <s>dharma</s>, knowledge (<s>jñāna</s>), and dispassion (<s>vairāgya</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "nārāyaṇaḥ paraṃ brahma gītāśāstre samīritaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 2,
          "translated_text": "is proclaimed in the teaching of the <s>Gītā</s>."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_1"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sva-dharma-jñāna-vairāgya-sādhya-bhakty-eka-gocaraḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nārāyaṇaḥ paraṃ brahma gītā-śāstre samīritaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_2",
        "label": "YGas 2"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "jñānakarmātmike niṣṭhe yogalakṣe susaṃskṛte |",
          "segment_number": 3,
          "translated_text": "The two commitments (<s>niṣṭhā</s>) — consisting of knowledge (<s>jñāna</s>) and action (<s>karma</s>), well-refined, having <s>yoga</s> as their aim —"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ātmānubhūtisiddhyārthe pūrvaṣaṭkena coditaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 4,
          "translated_text": "are taught in the first group of six [chapters] for the purpose of attaining the realization of the Self (<s>ātmānubhūti</s>)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_2"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jñāna-karma-ātmike niṣṭhe yoga-lakṣe su-saṃskṛte |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ātma-anubhūti-siddhya-arthe pūrva-ṣaṭkena coditaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_3",
        "label": "YGas 3"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "madhyame bhagavattattvayāthātmyāvāptisiddhaye |",
          "segment_number": 5,
          "translated_text": "In the middle [group of six chapters], for the attainment of the true nature of the <s>Bhagavat</s> (the Divine),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "jñānakarmābhinirvartyo bhaktiyogaḥ prakīrtitaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 6,
          "translated_text": "<s>bhaktiyoga</s> (the yoga of devotion), to be accomplished through knowledge and action, is proclaimed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_3"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "madhyame bhagavat-tattva-yāthātmya-avāpti-siddhaye |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jñāna-karma-abhinirvartyo bhakti-yogaḥ prakīrtitaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_4",
        "label": "YGas 4"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pradhānapuruṣavyaktasarveśvaravivecanam |",
          "segment_number": 7,
          "translated_text": "The discrimination between <s>pradhāna</s> (primordial matter), <s>puruṣa</s> (the individual soul), <s>vyakta</s> (the manifest), and the Lord of all (<s>sarveśvara</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "karma dhīr bhaktir ityādipūrvaśeṣo 'ntimoditaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 8,
          "translated_text": "action (<s>karma</s>), wisdom (<s>dhī</s>), devotion (<s>bhakti</s>), and the rest — the remainder of what precedes — is taught in the last [group of six chapters]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_4"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "pradhāna-puruṣa-vyakta-sarva-īśvara-vivecanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "karma dhīr bhaktir ity-ādi-pūrva-śeṣo 'ntima-uditaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_5",
        "label": "YGas 5"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "asthānasnehakāruṇyadharmādharmadhiyākulam |",
          "segment_number": 9,
          "translated_text": "Directed toward <s>Pārtha</s> (<s>Arjuna</s>), who had surrendered, confused by misplaced affection (<s>sneha</s>), pity (<s>kāruṇya</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pārthaṃ prapannam uddiśya śāstrāvatraṇaṃ kṛtam ||",
          "segment_number": 10,
          "translated_text": "and the [wrong] understanding of <s>dharma</s> and <s>adharma</s> — the descent of the scripture (<s>śāstra</s>) was made."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_5"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "asthāna-sneha-kāruṇya-dharma-adharma-dhiyā-kulam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "pārthaṃ prapannam uddiśya śāstra-avatraṇaṃ kṛtam ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_6",
        "label": "YGas 6"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "nityātmāsaṅgakarmehagocarā sāṃkhyayogadhīḥ |",
          "segment_number": 11,
          "translated_text": "The understanding of <s>Sāṃkhya</s> and <s>Yoga</s>, whose domain is the eternal Self, detached action, and this-worldly [goals],"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "dvitīye sthitadhīlakṣyā proktā tanmohaśāntaye ||",
          "segment_number": 12,
          "translated_text": "is taught in the second [chapter], aimed at [describing] the characteristics of one of steady wisdom (<s>sthitadhī</s>), for the pacification of his delusion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_6"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nitya-ātma-asaṅga-karma-iha-gocarā sāṃkhya-yoga-dhīḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "dvitīye sthita-dhī-lakṣyā proktā tan-moha-śāntaye ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_7",
        "label": "YGas 7"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "asaktyā lokarakṣāyai guṇeṣv āropya kartrktām |",
          "segment_number": 13,
          "translated_text": "Through detachment, for the protection of the world (<s>lokarakṣā</s>), assigning agency to the <s>guṇas</s> (qualities of nature)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "sarveśvare vā nyasyoktā tṛtīye karmakāryatā ||",
          "segment_number": 14,
          "translated_text": "or surrendering [it] to the Lord of all (<s>sarveśvara</s>) — the obligatory nature of action (<s>karmakāryatā</s>) is stated in the third [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_7"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "asaktyā loka-rakṣāyai guṇeṣv āropya kartrktām |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sarva-īśvare vā nyasya uktā tṛtīye karma-kāryatā ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_8",
        "label": "YGas 8"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "prasaṅgāt svasvabhāvoktiḥ karmaṇo 'karmatāsya ca |",
          "segment_number": 15,
          "translated_text": "Incidentally, the statement of [the Lord's] own nature, the non-action-ness (<s>akarmatā</s>) of action,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhedā jñānasya māhātmyam caturthādhyāya ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 16,
          "translated_text": "the varieties of knowledge and its greatness — are stated in the fourth chapter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_8"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "prasaṅgāt sva-svabhāva-uktiḥ karmaṇo 'karmata āsya ca |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhedā jñānasya māhātmyam caturtha-adhyāya ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_9",
        "label": "YGas 9"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "karmayogasya saukaryaṃ śaighryaṃ kāścana tadvidhāḥ |",
          "segment_number": 17,
          "translated_text": "The ease of <s>karmayoga</s> (the yoga of action), its swiftness, certain methods for its [practice],"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "brahmajñānprakāraś ca pañcamādhyāya ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 18,
          "translated_text": "and the manner of <s>Brahma</s>-knowledge — are stated in the fifth chapter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_9"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "karma-yogasya saukaryaṃ śaighryaṃ kāścana tad-vidhāḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "brahma-jñān-prakāraś ca pañcama-adhyāya ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_10",
        "label": "YGas 10"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yogābhyāsavidhir yogī caturdhā yogasādhanam |",
          "segment_number": 19,
          "translated_text": "The method of practicing <s>yoga</s>, the four types of <s>yogī</s>, the means of [attaining] <s>yoga</s>,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yogasiddhaḥ svayogasya pāramyaṃ ṣaṣṭha ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 20,
          "translated_text": "the <s>yoga</s>-adept (<s>yogasiddha</s>), and the supremacy of his own <s>yoga</s> — are stated in the sixth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_10"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yoga-abhyāsa-vidhir yogī caturdhā yoga-sādhanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yoga-siddhaḥ sva-yogasya pāramyaṃ ṣaṣṭha ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_11",
        "label": "YGas 11"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "svayāthātmyaṃ prakṛtyāsya tirodhiḥ śaraṇāgatiḥ |",
          "segment_number": 21,
          "translated_text": "[The Lord's] own true nature (<s>svayāthātmya</s>), the concealment by <s>prakṛti</s> (material nature), taking refuge (<s>śaraṇāgati</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhaktabhedaḥ prabuddhasya śraiṣṭhyaṃ saptama ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 22,
          "translated_text": "the types of devotees (<s>bhaktabheda</s>), and the excellence of the awakened one — are stated in the seventh [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_11"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sva-yāthātmyaṃ prakṛtya āsya tirodhiḥ śaraṇā-gatiḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhakta-bhedaḥ prabuddhasya śraiṣṭhyaṃ saptama ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_12",
        "label": "YGas 12"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "aiśvaryākṣarayāthātmyaṃ bhagavaccaraṇārthiṇām |",
          "segment_number": 23,
          "translated_text": "The true nature of sovereignty (<s>aiśvarya</s>) and the imperishable (<s>akṣara</s>); for those who seek the feet of the <s>Bhagavān</s>,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vedyopādeyabhāvānām aṣṭame bhede ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 24,
          "translated_text": "the distinction between what is to be known and what is to be chosen — is stated in the eighth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_12"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "aiśvarya-akṣara-yāthātmyaṃ bhagavac-caraṇa-arthiṇām |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "vedya-upādeya-bhāvānām aṣṭame bhede ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_13",
        "label": "YGas 13"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "svamāhātmyaṃ manuṣyatve paratvaṃ ca mahātmanām |",
          "segment_number": 25,
          "translated_text": "[The Lord's] own greatness, His supremacy even while in human form, and [the greatness] of noble souls,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "viśeṣo navame yogo bhaktirūpaḥ prakīrtitaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 26,
          "translated_text": "the special <s>yoga</s> in the form of <s>bhakti</s> (devotion) — is proclaimed in the ninth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_13"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sva-māhātmyaṃ manuṣyatve paratvaṃ ca mahā-ātmanām |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "viśeṣo navame yogo bhakti-rūpaḥ prakīrtitaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_14",
        "label": "YGas 14"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "svakalyāṇaguṇānantyakṛtsnasvādhīnatāmatiḥ |",
          "segment_number": 27,
          "translated_text": "[The Lord's] own infinite auspicious qualities, the understanding that all is entirely under His control —"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhaktyutpattivivṛdhyarthā vistīrṇā daśamoditā ||",
          "segment_number": 28,
          "translated_text": "[these,] expanded for the arising and growth of <s>bhakti</s>, are taught in the tenth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_14"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sva-kalyāṇa-guṇa-ānantya-kṛtsna-sva-adhīnatā-matiḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhakty-utpatti-vivṛdhy-arthā vistīrṇā daśama-uditā ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_15",
        "label": "YGas 15"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ekādaśe 'sya yāthātmyasākṣātkārāvalokanam |",
          "segment_number": 29,
          "translated_text": "In the eleventh [chapter], the direct vision (<s>sākṣātkāra</s>) of His true form (<s>yāthātmya</s>)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "dattam uktā vidiprāptyor bhaktyekopāyatā tathā ||",
          "segment_number": 30,
          "translated_text": "is granted, and it is stated that <s>bhakti</s> alone is the means of knowing and attaining [Him]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_15"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ekādaśe 'sya yāthātmya-sākṣātkāra-avalokanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "dattam uktā vidi-prāptyor bhakty-eka-upāyatā tathā ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_16",
        "label": "YGas 16"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhaktiśraiṣṭhyam upāyoktir aśaktasyātmaniṣṭhatā |",
          "segment_number": 31,
          "translated_text": "The excellence of <s>bhakti</s>, the statement of the means [for one who is capable], the establishment in the Self (<s>ātmaniṣṭhā</s>) for one who is incapable,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tatprakārās tv atiprītir bhakte dvādaśa ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 32,
          "translated_text": "the modes of that [practice], and the supreme love for the devotee — are stated in the twelfth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_16"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhakti-śraiṣṭhyam upāya-uktir aśaktasyā atma-niṣṭhatā |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tat-prakārās tv atiprītir bhakte dvādaśa ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_17",
        "label": "YGas 17"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "dehasvarūpam ātmāptihetur ātmaviśodhanam |",
          "segment_number": 33,
          "translated_text": "The nature of the body, the cause of attaining the Self (<s>ātmāpti</s>), the purification of the Self,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bandhahetur vivekaś ca trayodaśa udīryate ||",
          "segment_number": 34,
          "translated_text": "the cause of bondage, and discrimination (<s>viveka</s>) — are taught in the thirteenth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_17"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "deha-svarūpam ātma-āpti-hetur ātma-viśodhanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bandha-hetur vivekaś ca trayo-daśa udīryate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_18",
        "label": "YGas 18"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "guṇabandhavidhau teṣāṃ kartṛtvam tannivartanam |",
          "segment_number": 35,
          "translated_text": "The method of the bondage by the <s>guṇas</s> (qualities), their agency, the cessation of that [bondage],"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "gatitrayasvamūlatvaṃ caturdaśa udīryate ||",
          "segment_number": 36,
          "translated_text": "the three destinations (<s>gatitrayā</s>) and His being the root [of all] — are taught in the fourteenth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_18"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "guṇa-bandha-vidhau teṣāṃ kartṛtvam tan-nivartanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "gati-traya-sva-mūlatvaṃ catur-daśa udīryate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_19",
        "label": "YGas 19"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "acinmiśrād viśuddhāc ca cetanāt puruṣottamaḥ |",
          "segment_number": 37,
          "translated_text": "From the sentient mixed with the non-sentient, and from the pure sentient (<s>cetana</s>), the Supreme Person (<s>Puruṣottama</s>)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "vyāpānād bharaṇāt svāmyād anyaḥ pañcadaśoditaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 38,
          "translated_text": "is distinct by pervading, sustaining, and being the sovereign — this is taught in the fifteenth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_19"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "acin-miśrād viśuddhāc ca cetanāt puruṣa-uttamaḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "vyāpānād bharaṇāt svāmyād anyaḥ pañca-daśa-uditaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_20",
        "label": "YGas 20"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "devāsuravibhāgoktipūrvikā śāstravaśyatā |",
          "segment_number": 39,
          "translated_text": "Preceded by the statement of the divine and demonic natures, submission to scripture (<s>śāstravaśyatā</s>)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tattvānuṣṭhānavijñānasthemne ṣoḍaśa ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 40,
          "translated_text": "for the firm establishment of reality, practice, and knowledge — is stated in the sixteenth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_20"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "deva-asura-vibhāga-ukti-pūrvikā śāstra-vaśyatā |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tattva-anuṣṭhāna-vijñāna-sthemne ṣoḍaśa ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_21",
        "label": "YGas 21"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "aśāstram āsuraṃ kṛtsnam śāstrīyaṃ guṇataḥ pṛthak |",
          "segment_number": 41,
          "translated_text": "All that is non-scriptural is demonic (<s>āsura</s>); what is scriptural is distinguished according to the <s>guṇas</s>;"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "lakṣaṇaṃ śāstrasiddhasya tridhā saptadaśoditam ||",
          "segment_number": 42,
          "translated_text": "the characteristics of what is established by scripture in three ways — are taught in the seventeenth [chapter]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_21"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "aśāstram āsuraṃ kṛtsnam śāstrīyaṃ guṇataḥ pṛthak |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "lakṣaṇaṃ śāstra-siddhasya tridhā sapta-daśa-uditam ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_22",
        "label": "YGas 22"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "īśvare kartṛtābuddhiḥ sattvopādeyatāntime |",
          "segment_number": 43,
          "translated_text": "The understanding that agency belongs to the Lord (<s>Īśvara</s>), the preferability of <s>sattva</s> (goodness), in the last [chapter],"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "svakarmapariṇāmaś ca śāstrasārārtha ucyate ||",
          "segment_number": 44,
          "translated_text": "and the transformation of one's own <s>karma</s> — the essential meaning of the scripture is stated."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_22"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "īśvare kartṛtā-buddhiḥ sattva-upādeyatā-antime |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sva-karma-pariṇāmaś ca śāstra-sāra-artha ucyate ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_23",
        "label": "YGas 23"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "karmayogas tapastīrthadānayajñādisevanam |",
          "segment_number": 45,
          "translated_text": "<s>Karmayoga</s> (the yoga of action) is the practice of austerity (<s>tapas</s>), pilgrimage (<s>tīrtha</s>), charity (<s>dāna</s>), sacrifice (<s>yajña</s>), and the like."
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "jñānayogo jitasvāntaiḥ pariśuddhātmani sthitiḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 46,
          "translated_text": "<s>Jñānayoga</s> (the yoga of knowledge) is the establishment in the purified Self by those who have conquered their minds."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_23"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "karma-yogas tapas-tīrtha-dāna-yajña-ādi-sevanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jñāna-yogo jita-sva-antaiḥ pariśuddha-ātmani sthitiḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_24",
        "label": "YGas 24"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhaktiyogaḥ parāikāntyaprītyā dhyānādiṣu sthitiḥ |",
          "segment_number": 47,
          "translated_text": "<s>Bhaktiyoga</s> (the yoga of devotion) is the steadfast practice of meditation and the like with exclusive and ultimate love for the Supreme."
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "trayānām api yogānāṃ tribhir anyonyasaṃgamaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 48,
          "translated_text": "Each of the three <s>yogas</s> has a threefold interconnection with the [other] three."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_24"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhakti-yogaḥ para-aikāntya-prītyā dhyāna-ādiṣu sthitiḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "trayānām api yogānāṃ tribhir anyonya-saṃgamaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_25",
        "label": "YGas 25"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "nityanaimittikānāṃ ca parārādhanarūpiṇam |",
          "segment_number": 49,
          "translated_text": "The regular (<s>nitya</s>) and occasional (<s>naimittika</s>) [duties], having the form of worship of the Supreme (<s>parārādhana</s>),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ātmaṛṣṭes trayo 'py ete yogadvāreṇa sādhakāḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 50,
          "translated_text": "together with the purification of the Self — all three of these are means [of liberation] through the gateway of <s>yoga</s>."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_25"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nitya-naimittikānāṃ ca para-ārādhana-rūpiṇam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ātma-ṛṣṭes trayo 'py ete yoga-dvāreṇa sādhakāḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_26",
        "label": "YGas 26"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "nirastanikhilājñāno dṛṣṭvātmānaṃ parānugam |",
          "segment_number": 51,
          "translated_text": "Having removed all ignorance, seeing the Self as subordinate to the Supreme,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pratilabhya parāṃ bhaktiṃ tayaivāvāpnoti tatpadam ||",
          "segment_number": 52,
          "translated_text": "having attained supreme <s>bhakti</s> (devotion), by that alone one reaches His abode."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_26"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nirasta-nikhila-ajñāno dṛṣṭvā ātmānaṃ para-anugam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "pratilabhya parāṃ bhaktiṃ taya aiva avāpnoti tat-padam ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_27",
        "label": "YGas 27"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhaktiyogas tadarthī cet samagrāiśvaryasādhanam |",
          "segment_number": 53,
          "translated_text": "If one desires that [supreme abode], <s>bhaktiyoga</s> is the means of [attaining] complete sovereignty (<s>samagraiśvarya</s>);"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "ātmārthī cet trayo 'py ete tatkaivalyasya sādhakāḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 54,
          "translated_text": "if one desires the Self alone, all three of these are the means of its isolation (<s>kaivalya</s>)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_27"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhakti-yogas tad-arthī cet samagra-aiśvarya-sādhanam |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ātma-arthī cet trayo 'py ete tat-kaivalyasya sādhakāḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_28",
        "label": "YGas 28"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "aikāntyaṃ bhagavaty eṣāṃ samānam adhikāriṇām |",
          "segment_number": 55,
          "translated_text": "Exclusive devotion to the <s>Bhagavān</s> is common to all qualified [practitioners];"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yāvatprāpti parārthī cet tad evātyantam aśunute ||",
          "segment_number": 56,
          "translated_text": "if one seeks the ultimate, one attains that itself as permanent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_28"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "aikāntyaṃ bhagavaty eṣāṃ samānam adhikāriṇām |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yāvat-prāpti para-arthī cet tad eva atyantam aśunute ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_29",
        "label": "YGas 29"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "jñānī tu paramaikāntī tadāyattātmajīvanaḥ |",
          "segment_number": 57,
          "translated_text": "But the <s>jñānī</s> (the knower) is supremely exclusive, his very life depending on Him,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tatsaṃśleṣaviyogaikasukhaduḥkhas tadekadhīḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 58,
          "translated_text": "his sole happiness and sorrow being union with and separation from Him, his mind fixed on Him alone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_29"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jñānī tu parama-ekāntī tad-āyatta-ātma-jīvanaḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tat-saṃśleṣa-viyoga-eka-sukha-duḥkhas tad-eka-dhīḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_30",
        "label": "YGas 30"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "bhagavaddhyānayogoktivandanastutikīrtanaiḥ |",
          "segment_number": 59,
          "translated_text": "Through meditation on the <s>Bhagavān</s>, recitation, prostration, praise, and <s>kīrtana</s> (glorification),"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "labdhātmā tadgataprāṇamanobuddhīndriyakriyaḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 60,
          "translated_text": "having attained the Self, with his <s>prāṇa</s> (breath), mind, intellect, senses, and actions directed toward Him,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_30"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhagavad-dhyāna-yoga-ukti-vandana-stuti-kīrtanaiḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "labdha-ātmā tad-gata-prāṇa-mano-buddhi-indriya-kriyaḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_31",
        "label": "YGas 31"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "nijakarmādibhaktyantaṃ kuryāt prītyaiva kāritaḥ |",
          "segment_number": 61,
          "translated_text": "one should perform [everything] from one's own prescribed duties up to <s>bhakti</s>, motivated solely by love (<s>prīti</s>);"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "upāyatāṃ parityajya nyasyed deve tu tām abhīḥ ||",
          "segment_number": 62,
          "translated_text": "abandoning [the sense of] these being mere means (<s>upāyatā</s>), one should fearlessly surrender them to the Lord."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {
        "type": "analysis",
        "corresp": "#YGas_31"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nija-karma-ādi-bhakty-antaṃ kuryāt prītya aiva kāritaḥ |"
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "upāyatāṃ parityajya nyasyed deve tu tām abhīḥ ||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "YGas_32",
        "label": "YGas 32"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
